                      "text": "Identification: Long-bladed knife for soft-tissue division during amputation.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Main parts: Handle, blade, cutting edge, tip, and spine.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Principle: Sharp-force cutting.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Main uses: Soft-tissue division and flap formation.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Major risks: Haemorrhage, nerve injury, wound complications, and sharps injuries.",
                      "level": 0
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Key distinction: An amputation knife cuts soft tissue; a bone saw divides bone.",
                      "level": 0
                    }
                  ]
